From 68b16f02c76935989cc219f08a7aa7941cfd2afe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Hawkley <dan@triplettrustprotocol.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:05:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A3b: verified certificate checker and 116 more Lemma 7.10
 roots (412/455)

Adds a kernel-verified certificate checker for the packing conditions
(Solution/PackingCert.lean): sparse Farkas certificates over subdivision
trees of sorted cells, with soundness, permutation invariance of packing,
and the sorted base cell including the full (gamma, omega0) box of
Proposition 7.8 (D). The Challenge/Solution pair PackingB proves 116 more
roots of Lemma 7.10 (all remaining A, C, E roots and 47 of the 90 D
roots), one kernel check per certificate row, for 412 of 455 in total.
The 43 remaining D roots are listed in openRootsB.

Certificates are in specs/certificates/packing_a3b.json with their
generator and emitter; regeneration is byte-identical and the emitter's
--check confirms the Lean data equals the JSON.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DyEq5SJg3P8RhuwC4Kgon8
