+# Result record: seventh Challenge/Solution pair (A3b, Lemma 7.10 packing, second part)
+
+identity:
+  id: A3b
+  statement: "Lemma 7.10: 116 further packing roots by kernel-checked subdivision certificates; 412 of 455 proved in total"
+  source: "Source/bgp212.pdf: Definition 7.4 (p. 28), Proposition 7.8 (A)–(E) (pp. 31–32), Lemma 7.10 (p. 36)"
+  specification: specs/A0_parameters.yaml
+  builds_on: "A3a (BGP212/Packing.lean, Solution/Packing.lean), unchanged"
+
+state:
+  mathematical: proved          # for the 412 roots in settledRoots ++ settledRootsB
+  computational: kernel-verified
+  provenance: pinned
+  publication: draft
+
+verification:
+  challenge: Challenge/PackingB.lean
+  solution: Solution/PackingB.lean
+  checker: Solution/PackingCert.lean
+  certificate_data: [Solution/PackingBData.lean, Solution/PackingBCheck.lean]
+  ledger: BGP212/PackingLedgerB.lean
+  comparator_config: Comparator/packing_a3b.json
+  theorems:
+    packs_perm: "packing is invariant under permuting the coordinates"
+    root_ledger_b: "settledRootsB (116) ++ openRootsB (43) ~ A3a's openRoots; settledRoots ++ settledRootsB ++ openRootsB ~ allRoots (455)"
+    lemma_7_10_a3b: "each of the 116 roots holds for every profile in its domain; (D) uniformly over the full (γ, ω₀) box"
+    lemma_7_10_proved: "412 roots proved: settledRoots (A3a) ++ settledRootsB (A3b)"
+  roots_proved_in_a3b: { A: 31, C: 13, E: 25, D: 47, total: 116 }
+  checker_design: >
+    A certificate is a subdivision tree over a cell of linear constraints in the coordinates
+    v = sort↓(side 1) ++ sort↓(side 2) ++ extras (extras = [γ, ω₀] for (D)). The base cell
+    is: each side sorted decreasingly, its last coordinate ≥ δ, its sum ≤ B₁,ₘ; for (D) also
+    the box of Proposition 7.8. A split a·v ≤ b | −a·v ≤ −b covers its cell by trichotomy. A
+    leaf gives an assignment of the sorted coordinates to bins and, per bin, a sparse Farkas
+    certificate (nonnegative multipliers on the cell's constraints whose combination equals
+    the bin's load inequality exactly). checkTree_sound proves that a checked tree yields a
+    valid packing at every point of its cell; sortDesc and packs_perm carry it back to the
+    unsorted profile. Every rational in the data is re-checked by the kernel.
+  uniformity: >
+    The (D) roots quantify over every (γ, ω₀) in the box; the checker treats γ and ω₀ as
+    coordinates of v constrained by the box, so each leaf's Farkas certificate covers its
+    whole sub-box, and the split tree covers the box. No sampling enters the kernel proof.
+  certificates:
+    file: specs/certificates/packing_a3b.json
+    sha256: 75e9de9807a42a8ff44b706dd899e28e65574d5f49c7065a589843e71e3b1e09
+    generator: specs/checks/packing_a3b_generate.py   # exploratory; MILP proposes, Fractions re-verify
+    emitter: specs/checks/packing_a3b_emit.py         # JSON → Lean data; --check diffs against the repo
+    regeneration: "byte-identical on rerun (about 15 minutes); emitter --check reports match for all three Lean data files"
+    leaves: { A_C_E: "69 single-leaf trees", D: "518 leaves over 47 roots (γ, ω₀ bisection, depth ≤ 8)" }
+  exploratory_vs_proved: >
+    Exploratory: the generator (scipy.optimize.milp candidates, exact Fraction re-check) and
+    the emitter. Proved: the theorems above; the Lean kernel re-checks each of the 116 rows
+    (one theorem per row, about 2.5 minutes in total).
+  axioms_used: [propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice]
+  trusted_base: Lean 4 kernel + core library (Mathlib absent from this pair)
+  remaining_obligations:
+    open_roots: 43
+    list: "openRootsB in BGP212/PackingLedgerB.lean, all condition (D)"
+    pairs: "(1,3) (1,4) (2,2) (2,3) (2,4) (3,3)–(3,7) (4,4)–(4,8) (5,5)–(5,9) (6,6)–(6,10) (7,7)–(7,11) (8,8)–(8,11) (9,9)–(9,11) (10,10)–(10,12) (11,11) (11,12) (12,12)"
+    reason: "box-only bisection to depth 8 finds no single partition per sub-box; these roots need subdivision in profile space too"
+    plan: >
+      A3c: split on profile hyperplanes (the checker already accepts any split vector over
+      all coordinates), compute leaf multipliers by exact LP (closed forms cover product cells
+      only), and add an empty-cell node with a Farkas infeasibility certificate plus its
+      soundness lemma. The 455/455 ledger is claimed only after every root is verified.
+  negative_controls:
+    - change: "lemma_7_10_proved claims 413 roots in the Challenge"
+      result: "rejected: 'Challenge and solution theorem statement do not match: BGP212.Challenge.lemma_7_10_proved'"
+    - change: "lemma_7_10_a3b claimed for all 159 of A3a's openRoots in the Challenge"
+      result: "rejected: 'Challenge and solution theorem statement do not match: BGP212.Challenge.lemma_7_10_a3b'"
+    - change: "one Farkas multiplier of certificate row 85, root (D, 9, 12), changed by 1 in its numerator"
+      result: "kernel rejects: 'Tactic decide failed' for rowB of the corrupted row"
+    - change: "one coordinate of row 85's first leaf moved to another bin"
+      result: "kernel rejects: 'Tactic decide failed' for rowB of the corrupted row"
+    - change: "open root (D, 1, 3) moved from openRootsB into settledRootsB"
+      result: "Solution fails to build: root_ledger_b and certTableB_keys disproved by decide, lemma_7_10_a3b kernel error"
+  sandbox: >
+    Comparator ran with the pass-through landrun stand-in in the authoring environment.
+    Rerun ./verify.sh on the VPS with the real landrun to record a sandboxed result.
+
+result:
+  toolchain: leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2
+  comparator: leanprover/comparator @ c78dd72
+  lean4export: leanprover/lean4export @ 483e011
+  output_tail:
+    - "Running Lean default kernel on solution."
+    - "Lean default kernel accepts the solution"
+    - "Your solution is okay!"
+  verify_time: "about 7.5 minutes for all seven suites"
+  run_date: 2026-10-16
+  commit_hash: null   # set to the verified commit after the VPS run
+
+footer: Admissible generalizations trail leading specifications.
